1
00:05:17,500 --> 00:05:23,500
Discover the true story of one of America's
brightest stars... that faded too soon.

2
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:41,000
Selena is a drama, music, history film directed by Gregory Nava.

3
00:15:52,500 --> 00:15:58,500
In this biographical drama, Selena Quintanilla is born into
a musical Mexican-American family in Texas.

4
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:16,000
Her father, Abraham, realizes that his young daughter is talented
and begins performing with her at small venues.

5
00:26:27,500 --> 00:26:33,500
She finds success and falls for her guitarist, Chris
Perez, who draws the ire of her father.

6
00:31:45,000 --> 00:31:51,000
Seeking mainstream stardom, Selena begins recording an
English-language album which, tragically, she would never complete.

7
00:37:02,500 --> 00:37:08,500
Selena Quintanilla, played by Jennifer Lopez.

8
00:42:20,000 --> 00:42:26,000
Suzette Quintanilla, played by Jackie Guerra.

9
00:47:37,500 --> 00:47:43,500
Marcela Quintanilla, played by Constance Marie.

10
00:52:55,000 --> 00:53:01,000
Sara, played by Alex Meneses.

11
00:58:12,500 --> 00:58:18,500
Chris Perez, played by Jon Seda.

12
01:03:30,000 --> 01:03:36,000
Abraham Quintanilla, played by Edward James Olmos.

13
01:08:47,500 --> 01:08:53,500
Selena is a 1997 American biographical musical drama film about Tejano
music star Selena Quintanilla-Pérez, played by Jennifer Lopez.

14
01:14:05,000 --> 01:14:11,000
The film, written and directed by Gregory Nava, chronicles the star's rise to fame
and death when she was murdered by Yolanda Saldívar at the age of 23.

15
01:19:22,500 --> 01:19:28,500
In addition to Lopez, the film also stars Edward James Olmos, Jon Seda, Constance
Marie, Jacob Vargas, Lupe Ontiveros, and Jackie Guerra in her film debut.

16
01:24:40,000 --> 01:24:46,000
Selena was released in the United States on March 21, 1997, by Warner Bros.

17
01:29:57,500 --> 01:30:03,500
The film received positive reviews from critics and grossed $35 million
worldwide against a production budget of $20 million.

18
01:35:15,000 --> 01:35:21,000
For her performance, Jennifer Lopez received a Best Actress
nomination at the 55th Golden Globe Awards.

19
01:40:32,500 --> 01:40:38,500
In 2021, it was selected for preservation in the United States National Film Registry by the Library of Congress as being "culturally, historically,
or aesthetically significant", and was re-released in select cinemas on April 7, 2022, to coincide with the film's 25th anniversary.

20
01:45:50,000 --> 01:45:56,000
In 2024, the Pérez Art Museum Miami organized a screening of Selena as part
of the institution's Floating Films with Ballyhoo Media.

21
01:51:07,500 --> 01:51:13,500
During this event, the film was screened from the water.

22
01:56:25,000 --> 01:56:31,000
The film explores themes of texas, biography, elopement, bustier, fan club.

23
02:01:42,500 --> 02:01:48,500
The tone is emotional.
